         }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CGI versions from 4.62 before 5.00 for Perl allow cross-site scripting via a raw apostrophe in URLs returned by url and self_url.\n\nBoth pass the URL through URI's canonical method, which leaves an apostrophe in the path raw and decodes the %27 that query parameter escaping produces, so an apostrophe in the request path or a parameter appears raw in the result.\n\nAn application that places the URL in a single-quoted HTML attribute or JavaScript string is open to cross-site scripting.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
